LineageOS 15.1 sepolicy split — vendor side.

In Oreo the build system routes BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS into the vendor
policy compiled into /vendor/etc/selinux/nonplat_*.  For the m681
semi-treble build the existing flat .te files in the parent directory
cover all required vendor domain rules (connectivity.te, modem_daemons.te,
nvram_agent_binder.te, etc.).

When migrating to a full vendor split:
  - Move vendor-domain .te files here.
  - Keep platform-domain .te files in ../plat/.
  - Update BOARD_PLAT_SEPOLICY_DIRS and BOARD_SEPOLICY_DIRS accordingly.
